Usage: which [OPTION]... COMMAND...

Locate COMMAND in PATH.

OPTIONS:
  -a, --all             print all matching pathnames of each argument
  -v, --version         print version information
  -s, --silent          suppress all normal output
      --quiet           suppress all normal output
      --skip-dot        skip directories in PATH that start with a dot
      --skip-tilde      skip directories in PATH that start with a tilde and
                        HOME matches
      --show-dot        if a directory in PATH starts with a dot, print
                        ./COMMAND
      --show-tilde      output a tilde for the HOME directory
      --tty-only        only show results on a terminal
      --read-alias      read list of aliases from stdin
      --skip-alias      do not read aliases
      --read-functions  read shell functions from stdin
      --skip-functions  do not read shell functions
      --help            display this help and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
